{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanTraceConventionSplit"],"declarations":42,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trC_borromean_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trC_borromean_derived","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L342-L364","doc":"**MAIN: the canonical Markov trace of `β_Bor`, derived.**  Summing\nthe three per-block characters at `β_Bor` (both 1-dims `= 1` by\n`oneDim_chi_borromean`; the 2-dim `= 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` by\n`sn21_chi_borromean`) against the Markov-forced weights yields exactly\nthe convention-C closed form `trC_borromean t` of\n`BorromeanTraceConventionSplit`:\n\n    `w₃·1 + w₂₁·(2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶) + w₁₁₁·1 = trC_borromean t`,\n    `h = t² − t⁻²`.\n\nTogether with `conventionD_ne_conventionC` this machine-checks the full\nregistry claim: the canonical trace value at `β_Bor` is derived, and it\ndiffers exactly from the pipeline (TL/Jones) value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_markov_sigma0_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_markov_sigma0_sigma1","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L329-L340","doc":"**(M2, level 2)**: with `χ^λ(σ₀σ₁)` equal to `q² = t⁴`, `−1`\n(`sn21_trace_sigma0_sigma1`), `q⁻² = t⁻⁴` on the three blocks, the\nweighted sum equals `z²` — the Markov-forced `tr(σ₀σ₁) = z·tr(σ₀) = z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_markov_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_markov_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L315-L327","doc":"**(M2) Single-generator value**: with `χ^λ(σ)` equal to `q = t²`,\n`h = t² − t⁻²`, `−q⁻¹ = −t⁻²` on the three blocks respectively\n(`sn21_trace_sigma0` for the middle one), the weighted sum equals `z` —\nthe Markov-forced `tr(σᵢ) = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weights_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L305-L313","doc":"**(M3) Normalisation**: `w₃·χ³(1) + w₂₁·χ²¹(1) + w₁₁₁·χ^(1³)(1)\n= w₃ + 2w₂₁ + w₁₁₁ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weight_system_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weight_system_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L292-L303","doc":"**Nonsingularity of the Markov weight system.**  The determinant of\nthe 3×3 system `{Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(x) = tr(x)}` over `x ∈ {1, σ, σ₀σ₁}`\nequals `−(t⁴+1)(t²−t+1)(t²+t+1)(t⁴−t²+1)/t⁶`, nonzero for every\n`t ≠ 0` — so the three Markov-forced values pin the weights uniquely\n(Cramer). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L290-L290","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden_pos","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L284-L288","doc":"The common weight denominator is strictly positive, hence nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weight_den_factors_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weight_den_factors_pos","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L274-L282","doc":"All cyclotomic-type factors in the weight denominators are strictly\npositive over `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq111","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L271-L272","doc":"Weight of the sign block `(1³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq21","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L268-L269","doc":"Weight of the 2-dim block `(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wq3","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L264-L266","doc":"Weight of the trivial block `(3)` — unique solution of the\nMarkov-forced linear system (see `weight_system_det_ne_zero`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum111","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L260-L262","doc":"Numerator of the sign-block weight `w₁₁₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum21","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L254-L258","doc":"Numerator of the 2-dim-block weight `w₂₁` (over the COMMON\ndenominator `wden`, hence the extra `(t⁴+1)` factor relative to the\nfully-reduced form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wnum3","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L250-L252","doc":"Numerator of the trivial-block weight `w₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wden","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L245-L248","doc":"Common denominator of the Markov-forced weights:\n`D(t) = (t²+1)²(t⁴+1)(t²−t+1)(t²+t+1)(t⁴−t²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zMarkov","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L215-L243","doc":"The Markov parameter `z = 1/(√q + 1/√q) = t/(t² + 1)`.\n\n**Convention C, deliberately — this one is NOT migrated (2026-08-26, bean\n`qou-cxjq`).** Every other convention-C Markov parameter in the Lean tree moved\nto `z_D = q³/(q²+1)` under the owner ruling of 2026-08-15. This one stays,\nbecause the file exists to derive the **C** value: `trC_borromean_derived`\nevaluates the C-forced weight system at `β_Bor` and lands on `trC_borromean`,\nwhich `BorromeanTraceConventionSplit.conventionD_ne_conventionC` then proves is\na different function from the D closed form. Migrate `z` here and the file\nderives the D trace and compares it to itself — the registry claim it exists to\nmachine-check evaporates.\n\nThe whole apparatus below is C-forced and moves with it: `wden`, `wnum3`,\n`wnum21`, `wnum111` are the solution of the 3×3 Markov system at *this* `z`\n(`weights_markov_sigma` closes the loop by recovering `zMarkov t` from them), so\nthey are not shared constants that survive a convention change — they are C's\nanswer to C's system.\n\n**Why the audit called this actionable, and why that was a detector limit rather\nthan a defect.** `scripts/lean-markov-convention-audit.py` takes deliberateness\nevidence from the declaration's name and its own docstring. This module's intent\nwas stated only in the **module header** — its first line reads *\"Canonical\n(convention C) Markov trace of β_Bor\"* — and in `trC_borromean_derived`'s\ndocstring three declarations below. A detector that walks back from a\ndeclaration to the doc-comment opener directly above it cannot see either. Recorded as entry #16 in the\ndetector-blindness taxonomy; fixed at the source, here, rather than by teaching\nthe scanner to trust module headers, which would silently absolve every C\ndefinition in any file whose header mentions C. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.oneDim_chi_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.oneDim_chi_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L202-L209","doc":"The two 1-dim characters at `β_Bor` are both `1`: `σᵢ ↦ q` sends\n`(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³ ↦ (q·q⁻¹)³ = 1`, and `σᵢ ↦ −q⁻¹` likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_chi_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_chi_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L188-L200","doc":"**χ^(2,1)(β_Bor) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶** — the 2-dim character of the\nBorromean braid `β_Bor = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`, machine-checked: with\n`P = σ₀σ₁⁻¹`, `τ = tr P = −1 − h²` and `δ = det P = 1`\n(`sn21_trace_borP`, `sn21_det_borP`), the Cayley–Hamilton cube identity\ngives `tr(P³) = τ³ − 3τ = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_det_borP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_det_borP","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L181-L186","doc":"The Borromean word factor `P := σ₀·σ₁⁻¹` has determinant `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_borP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_borP","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L172-L179","doc":"The Borromean word factor `P := σ₀·σ₁⁻¹`: trace `−1 − h²` (for\n`q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_sigma0_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_sigma0_sigma1","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L165-L170","doc":"Character of `σ₀σ₁`: `tr(σ₀·σ₁) = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_trace_sigma0","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L157-L163","doc":"Character of a single generator: `tr(σ₀) = h = q − q⁻¹` (eigenvalue\ncontent `{q, −q⁻¹}`).  `σ₁` is conjugate to `σ₀` (braid relation), so it\nhas the same character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_hecke_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_hecke_sigma1","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L150-L155","doc":"**Hecke quadratic for `σ₁`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_hecke_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_hecke_sigma0","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L141-L148","doc":"**Hecke quadratic for `σ₀`**: `σ₀² = h·σ₀ + 1` entrywise, i.e. the\npair descends to `H_3(q)`.  Stated entrywise to avoid extra algebraic\nstructure on `M2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_braid","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L133-L139","doc":"**Braid relation** `σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁` — the pair is a `B_3`\nrepresentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L127-L131","doc":"`σ₁ · σ₁⁻¹ = 1` (for `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1_inv","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L123-L125","doc":"`σ₁⁻¹` in the 2-dim representation: `[−q, 1; 0, q⁻¹]`.  Equals the\nHecke inverse `σ₁ − h·1` entrywise: `−q⁻¹ − h = −q` and `q − h = q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma1","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L120-L121","doc":"`σ₁` in the rational seminormal 2-dim representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sn21_sigma0","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L117-L118","doc":"`σ₀` in the rational seminormal 2-dim representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.trace_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.trace_cube","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton cube identity**: `tr(X³) = τ³ − 3τδ` with\n`τ = tr X`, `δ = det X`.  Raw entry expansion + `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.det","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L99-L100","doc":"Determinant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.trace","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanCanonicalTraceDerivation.lean#L96-L97","doc":"Trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.one","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc